* Provenance: derived for circsim from datasheet-class forward-voltage targets by scripts/fit-model-cards.mjs, MIT.
* In-house LED .model cards. An LED is a diode whose forward drop is set by its
* die material; the datasheet typical Vf at the rated test current is reproduced
* by fitting the saturation current is, with the emission coefficient n, the
* series resistance rs and the bandgap eg held at class values (eg shifts the
* temperature behavior toward the wider-gap III-V material; n and rs set the
* slope of the knee; blue and white use n=2.2 because ngspice stops tracking the
* requested current once the internal junction voltage passes about 60 n*Vt).
* Nothing is read from any third-party library card.
*
* Target forward drops (typical @ ~20 mA) and the fitted value (the middle of
* each band, hit to within a few millivolts at 20 mA):
*   red    ~1.8-2.0 V  -> 1.90 V  (AlGaInP / GaAsP)
*   green  ~2.1-2.2 V  -> 2.15 V  (InGaN, traditional green ~2.2 V)
*   blue   ~3.0-3.2 V  -> 3.10 V  (InGaN)
*   white  ~3.0-3.4 V  -> 3.20 V  (blue InGaN die + phosphor)
* The 10 mA drop follows from n and rs (about 50 mV below the 20 mA value for red,
* 60 mV green, 100 mV blue, 110 mV white). Both points are checked by the
* led-*-vf-20ma and led-*-vf-10ma rows in resources/models/characterization.json
* (npm run test:characterization), so the targets above are enforced by CI.
*
* Cj is set ~15-50 pF (small indicator LED). Reverse Vbr ~5 V typical.

* --------------------------------------------------------------------------- RED
.model LED_RED D(is=8.51e-21 rs=2 n=1.7 cjo=30p vj=0.75 m=0.333 bv=5 ibv=100u
+ eg=1.9 xti=3)

* --------------------------------------------------------------------------- GREEN
.model LED_GREEN D(is=6.38e-22 rs=3 n=1.8 cjo=30p vj=0.75 m=0.333 bv=5
+ ibv=100u eg=2.1 xti=3)

* --------------------------------------------------------------------------- BLUE
.model LED_BLUE D(is=3.61e-25 rs=6 n=2.2 cjo=20p vj=0.75 m=0.333 bv=5 ibv=100u
+ eg=2.9 xti=3)

* --------------------------------------------------------------------------- WHITE
.model LED_WHITE D(is=8.84e-26 rs=7 n=2.2 cjo=20p vj=0.75 m=0.333 bv=5
+ ibv=100u eg=3 xti=3)
